---
import FamilyMotif from './FamilyMotif.astro';
import Mark from './Mark.astro';
const families = [
  { id: 'inside-a-service', name: 'Inside a service', text: 'Domain, use case, persistence and the gateways at a service’s edge, each with the test that proves it.', href: '/patterns/inside-a-service/domain/' },
  { id: 'between-services', name: 'Between services', text: 'Contracts, webhooks, idempotency and deploy gates for services owned by different teams.', href: '/patterns/between-services/' },
  { id: 'across-teams', name: 'Across teams', text: 'Platforms, team interaction and ways of working that let several teams ship one product.', href: '/patterns/across-teams/' },
];
---
<section class="cover not-content">
  <div class="big-mark"><Mark size={320} /></div>
  <h1>Every boundary is the same problem at a different scale.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Practical patterns for where code, services and teams meet. One running example, a coffee subscription, from a single function to the organisation.</p>
  <p class="actions"><a href="/start/the-coffee-subscription/">Meet the example</a><a href="/journeys/build-one-service-testably/">Follow a journey</a></p>
  <ul class="families">
    {families.map((f) => (
      <li>
        <a href={f.href}>
          <FamilyMotif family={f.id} size={120} />
          <h2>{f.name}</h2>
          <p>{f.text}</p>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p class="take-part">The catalogue grows with its readers. <a href="https://github.com/all-boundaries/website">Propose a pattern or correct a page</a>.</p>
</section>
<style>
  .cover { position: relative; max-width: 75rem; margin-inline: auto; padding: 4rem var(--sl-content-pad-x) 6rem; }
  .big-mark { position: absolute; right: var(--sl-content-pad-x); top: 4rem; color: var(--sl-color-white); display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) { .big-mark { display: block; } }
  .cover :global(svg) { width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .big-mark { width: clamp(14rem, 24vw, 22rem); }
  .families :global(svg) { width: 7.5rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 7vw, 6rem); font-weight: 800; line-height: 0.98; letter-spacing: -0.035em; max-width: 14ch; text-wrap: balance; color: var(--sl-color-white); margin: 0; }
  .lede { font-family: var(--ab-serif); font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 38rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0; color: var(--sl-color-white); }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem 2.5rem; margin: 2rem 0 0; font-weight: 700; }
  .actions a { white-space: nowrap; }
  .actions a, .take-part a { color: var(--sl-color-white); text-decoration: none; background: linear-gradient(var(--sl-color-accent), var(--sl-color-accent)) left bottom / 100% 4px no-repeat; padding-bottom: 0.2rem; transition: background-size 120ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .actions a, .take-part a { transition: none; } }
  .actions a:hover, .take-part a:hover { background-size: 100% 100%; color: #fff; }
  .families { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 5rem 0 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); column-gap: 2.5rem; row-gap: 3rem; border-top: 6px solid var(--sl-color-white); }
  .families a { display: block; padding-top: 2rem; color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .families h2 { font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; border: 0; }
  .families p { font-family: var(--ab-serif); margin: 0; max-width: 24rem; color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); }
  .families a:hover h2 { text-decoration: underline 4px var(--sl-color-accent); text-underline-offset: 0.3rem; }
  .take-part { margin: 4rem 0 0; font-family: var(--ab-serif); }
</style>
